     "text": "My friend’s dad built a business from nothing. 30 years. Blood and sweat. Turned it into something worth $2,000,000.\n\nSold it in 2019 to a private equity firm.\n\nThey gutted it in 18 months. Cut 40 jobs. Raised prices 35%. Eliminated the pension plan he’d built for his employees. Squeezed every dollar out and sold the carcass.\n\nHe calls it the worst decision he ever made. Said he thought they’d protect what he built.\n\nPrivate equity doesn’t buy businesses to run them. They buy them to harvest them. And they’re doing it to every industry you depend on daily.",
